The key part about these histograms is the highlighted (darker area with the lines) portion. 
The highlighted portion represents teams that have made the playoffs.  
Using these histograms it is a quick comparison of how playoof teams performed in particular stats versuses teams that did not make the playoffs.

Above the histograms is a box plot graph that will show dots.  These dots represent any outliers.  
